  <h2>Data we collect</h2>
  <p>CryptoBonusWorld does not require a user account for ordinary public browsing. The following data may be processed through site infrastructure or third-party tools:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Analytics and technical data</strong> — aggregated or pseudonymous information such as page views, referral source, browser or device information may be processed by analytics or hosting tools used by the site.</li>
    <li><strong>Affiliate click attribution</strong> — when you follow an affiliate link, the destination exchange or partner platform may use cookies, identifiers or tracking parameters to attribute a registration or other qualifying action.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies and local browser storage</h2>
  <p>
    The site may use browser storage for product preferences such as selected country or language, and third-party providers may use cookies or similar technologies according to their own policies. Browser controls can be used to clear or restrict stored data.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    CryptoBonusWorld links to exchanges and other third-party services. Those services control their own data processing and privacy practices. Review the privacy policy of the destination service before creating an account or providing personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    CryptoBonusWorld does not operate a public user-account database for ordinary site visitors. Any analytics, hosting or affiliate-attribution data is retained according to the configuration and policies of the relevant provider and applicable requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on your jurisdiction and the data involved, you may have rights relating to access, correction, deletion, restriction or objection. For privacy-related questions about CryptoBonusWorld, use the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>. Requests concerning an exchange or third-party platform should be directed to that provider.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy when the site's data practices, infrastructure or legal requirements change. The current version is published on this page.</p>
